	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>Command change numeric value ( Part 6 - F.22 )</h1>

<p>This command is used to change the value of an object. It applies only to objects that have a numeric value attribute. This FB is an AUDI adapter wrapper around <strong>Q_NumericValue</strong> — the same object-type validity rules apply.</p>

<h2>Valid Object IDs</h2>

<p>u16ObjId is valid if it falls within one of the following ISO 11783-6 ID ranges (see Q_NumericValue, Annex F.22):</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>InputBooleanField</strong>: 7000 – 7999</li>
	<li><strong>InputNumberField</strong>: 9000 – 9999</li>
	<li><strong>InputListField</strong>: 10000 – 10999</li>
	<li><strong>OutputNumberField</strong>: 12000 – 12999</li>
	<li><strong>Meter</strong>: 17000 – 17999</li>
	<li><strong>LinearBarGraph</strong>: 18000 – 18999</li>
	<li><strong>ArchedBarGraph</strong>: 19000 – 19999</li>
	<li><strong>NumberVariable</strong>: 21000 – 21999</li>
	<li><strong>ObjectPointer</strong>: 27000 – 27999</li>
	<li><strong>OutputListObject</strong>: 37000 – 37999</li>
	<li><strong>ExternalObjectPointer</strong>: 43000 – 43999</li>
	<li><strong>AnimationObject</strong>: 44000 – 44999</li>
	<li><strong>ScaledGraphicObject</strong>: 48000 – 48999</li>
</ul>

<p>ID_NULL (65535) is not a command target but can be used in INIT to deactivate the FB. Any ID outside these ranges is invalid for commanding.</p>

<h2>param[in] {objectID, uint16_t}</h2>

<p>Object ID</p>

<h2>param[in] {value, uint32_t}</h2>

<p>New value of ID</p>

<h2>Return Values:&nbsp;</h2>

<h3>int16_t</h3>

<ul>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NO_ERR (0)</span>&nbsp;- OK</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_OVERFLOW (-6)</span>&nbsp;- buffer overflow</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NOACT (-8)</span> - Command not possible in current state</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NO_INSTANCE (-21)</span>&nbsp;- No VT client available</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_ISO_INSTANCE_INVALID (-129)</span> - Identifier for instance (connection) invalid</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_HANDLE_INVALID</span><span style="color:#2980b9"> (-128)</span> - ErrorCause: invalid Handle</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NOT_ALIVE (-130)</span> - Identifier for instance valid, but VT Dead.</li>
</ul>
]]></Attribute>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
</FBType>
